Based on your interests in programming, mathematics, logical thinking, and your career preferences for Data Scientist, Developer, or Product Manager, here are three excellent universities in the UK or EU and one specific Bachelor's program at each that would be a strong fit:

    Imperial College London (UK)

+ Program: BEng Computing[1][2][3]

        Why it fits: Imperial is a world-leading science and technology university. This 3-year Bachelor of Engineering program focuses heavily on the fundamental principles and practical engineering aspects of computing, including hardware, software, and the underlying mathematics.[3] It emphasizes building complex, working systems, which aligns well with your interest in programming and problem-solving. Graduates are highly sought after in tech industries.

  University College London (UCL) (UK)[4]

+ Program: BSc Computer Science[5][6][7][8][9][10]

        Why it fits: UCL is another top-ranked global university with a highly regarded Computer Science department. This 3-year Bachelor of Science program provides a strong foundation in computer science theory (computation, algorithms, programming principles, discrete mathematics) combined with practical, real-world problem-solving.[10] It prepares graduates for diverse roles in the tech industry, including development and data science, and offers opportunities to specialize later on.

  Delft University of Technology (TU Delft) (Netherlands - EU)[4]

+ Program: BSc Computer Science and Engineering[8][11][12][13]

       Why it fits: TU Delft is a premier European technical university. This 3-year, English-taught Bachelor of Science program focuses on developing software and data processing for intelligent systems.[11] It covers mathematical analysis, logical reasoning, algorithms, programming, and software engineering, directly matching your interests. The program includes project work and touches upon areas like Data Science, Software Engineering, and Human-Computer Interaction, offering paths towards Data Scientist or Developer roles.

